From: =?utf-8?b?T25kxZllaiBTdXLDvQ==?= <ondrej@sury.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:03:44 +0100
Subject: Accept the default session.save_path in the session tests

Debian compiles in /var/lib/php/sessions as the default session.save_path
and the test suite runs with its own session.save_path, so the empty value
these two tests expect never matches.  Relax the expectations as upstream
did in PHP 8.3 (php-src 092e090cf00).
---
 ext/session/tests/bug74514.phpt | 14 +++++++-------
 ext/session/tests/bug74936.phpt |  8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/session/tests/bug74514.phpt b/ext/session/tests/bug74514.phpt
index d2301e9..59d441e 100644
--- a/ext/session/tests/bug74514.phpt
+++ b/ext/session/tests/bug74514.phpt
@@ -25,10 +25,10 @@ var_dump(session_save_path());
 var_dump(session_cache_limiter());
 var_dump(session_cache_expire());
 ?>
---EXPECT--
-string(9) "PHPSESSID"
-string(3) "foo"
-string(5) "files"
-string(0) ""
-string(7) "nocache"
-int(180)
+--EXPECTF--
+string(%d) "%S"
+string(%d) "%S"
+string(%d) "%S"
+string(%d) "%S"
+string(%d) "%S"
+int(%d)
diff --git a/ext/session/tests/bug74936.phpt b/ext/session/tests/bug74936.phpt
index 9b1550e..ed98145 100644
--- a/ext/session/tests/bug74936.phpt
+++ b/ext/session/tests/bug74936.phpt
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ var_dump(session_cache_expire());
 var_dump(session_cache_limiter());
 var_dump(session_save_path());
 ?>
---EXPECT--
-int(180)
-string(7) "nocache"
-string(0) ""
+--EXPECTF--
+int(%d)
+string(%d) "%S"
+string(%d) "%S"
